      {
        "body": "A 2×2 matrix multiplies a column. The sample mean is the sum of the observations divided by n.",
        "heading": "Mathematics — linear algebra and statistics",
        "math": [
          "\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix} ax+by \\\\ cx+dy \\end{pmatrix}",
          "\\det\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}=ad-bc",
          "\\bar{x}=\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}",
          "\\sigma^{2}=\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(x_{i}-\\bar{x})^{2}"
        ],
        "type": "prose"
      },
      {
        "body": "For constant acceleration, displacement, velocity, and time are related by the SUVAT set. The x–t graph is a curve; the v–t graph is a line.",
